rden-crossed-200000-in-annual-revenue/articleshow/134716786.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-canadian-couple-started-aslan-organics-with-two-8-by-12-foot-plots-in-2017-nine-years-later-they-own-a-50-acre-ontario-farm-and-say-their-2-5-acre-market-garden-crossed-200000-in-annual-revenue/articleshow/134716786.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T02:17:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134716808,imgsize-1394356.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US F-1 visa: Indian student claims October interview date got canceled for refusing to pay agent extra ₹20,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134716804.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-f-1-visa-indian-student-claims-october-interview-date-got-canceled-for-refusing-to-pay-agent-extra-20000/articleshow/134716804.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-f-1-visa-indian-student-claims-october-interview-date-got-canceled-for-refusing-to-pay-agent-extra-20000/articleshow/134716804.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T02:17:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134716811,imgsize-100430.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Montana meltdown: MAGA attacks Indians teaching at Montana State University. Turns out they are the 'best of the best']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134716611.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/montana-meltdown-maga-attacks-indians-teaching-at-montana-state-university-turns-out-they-are-the-best-of-the-best/articleshow/134716611.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/montana-meltdown-maga-attacks-indians-teaching-at-montana-state-university-turns-out-they-are-the-best-of-the-best/articleshow/134716611.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T01:15:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134716629,imgsize-41742.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Montana will never be the same': Who is Governor Greg Gianforte, the new target of MAGA's anti-India hatred?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134716230.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/montana-will-never-be-the-same-who-is-governor-greg-gianforte-the-new-target-of-magas-anti-india-hatred/articleshow/134716230.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/montana-will-never-be-the-same-who-is-governor-greg-gianforte-the-new-target-of-magas-anti-india-hatred/articleshow/134716230.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T00:46:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134716368,imgsize-53548.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pakistan, Saudi, Turkiye activate Mecca defence pact as Yemen war escalates]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134716048.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pakistan, Saudi Arabia, and Turkiye have agreed to enhance military cooperation to address regional security threats. Following recent attacks by Yemen's Houthi group, the three countries will activate collective deterrence measures. The emergency meeting of the Mecca Defence Alliance in Riyadh led to this commitment. Saudi-backed forces are also launching an offensive against the Houthis in Yemen to regain control.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/pakistan-saudi-arabia-turkiye-activate-mecca-defence-pact-amid-houthi-attacks/articleshow/134716048.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/pakistan-saudi-arabia-turkiye-activate-mecca-defence-pact-amid-houthi-attacks/articleshow/134716048.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T00:34:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134716118,imgsize-147712.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Not now daal-ing, says MAGA, as Montana governor comes to India to sell pulses]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134715572.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Montana's Governor Greg Gianforte is heading a delegation to India to promote agricultural exports. The focus is on selling lentils, peas, and chickpeas to the world's largest consumer of pulses. This trip highlights the growing tension within the Republican party regarding international trade and immigration. Many in the GOP criticize Gianforte's outreach to India amidst concerns about jobs for Americans.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/not-now-daal-ing-says-maga-as-montana-governor-comes-to-india-to-sell-pulses/articleshow/134715572.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/not-now-daal-ing-says-maga-as-montana-governor-comes-to-india-to-sell-pulses/articleshow/134715572.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T00:14:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chidanand Rajghatta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134715650,imgsize-177014.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Simon Andriesz: UK whistleblower who flagged Howard Lutnick’s alleged Epstein links dies by suicide, friend sets up fundraiser for son]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134713800.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/simon-andriesz-uk-whistleblower-who-flagged-howard-lutnicks-alleged-epstein-links-dies-by-suicide-friend-sets-up-fundraiser-for-son/articleshow/134713800.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/simon-andriesz-uk-whistleblower-who-flagged-howard-lutnicks-alleged-epstein-links-dies-by-suicide-friend-sets-up-fundraiser-for-son/articleshow/134713800.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T23:03:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134713875,imgsize-52144.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California family’s 6,625-acre ranch is now protected forever]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134675875.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Kinsey family has strategically safeguarded their vast 6,625-acre ranch in Benbow, California, by implementing a conservation easement. This crucial step preserves the land's agricultural, forest, and wildlife values, ensuring the ranch's ongoing functionality while protecting vital habitats for endangered species. David Johnson, a family member, was instrumental in this initiative, with the Northcoast Regional Land Trust planning to acknowledge their dedication to conservation this coming October.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1914-a-california-family-bought-what-became-the-6625-acre-kinsey-ranch-112-years-later-after-one-brother-pushed-to-protect-it-before-his-death-the-entire-working-cattle-ranch-is-now-permanently-protected-from-development/articleshow/134675875.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1914-a-california-family-bought-what-became-the-6625-acre-kinsey-ranch-112-years-later-after-one-brother-pushed-to-protect-it-before-his-death-the-entire-working-cattle-ranch-is-now-permanently-protected-from-development/articleshow/134675875.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T02:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134675949,imgsize-557110.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After losing her mother to MS, J.K. Rowling gave £10m to research]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134674141.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[J.K. Rowling opened the Anne Rowling Regenerative Neurology Clinic in memory of her mother, who died of multiple sclerosis. The clinic focuses on research and treatment of various neurological diseases, including multiple sclerosis and Parkinson's disease. The funding aims to attract world-class researchers to develop new therapies and potentially find a cure. It has already hosted numerous clinical appointments and research projects since its inception.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/j-k-rowling-lost-her-mother-to-multiple-sclerosis-at-45-in-2010-she-donated-10-million-for-an-edinburgh-research-clinic-in-her-mothers-name-and-the-facility-now-helps-thousands-of-people-with-brain-conditions/articleshow/134674141.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/j-k-rowling-lost-her-mother-to-multiple-sclerosis-at-45-in-2010-she-donated-10-million-for-an-edinburgh-research-clinic-in-her-mothers-name-and-the-facility-now-helps-thousands-of-people-with-brain-conditions/articleshow/134674141.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134674141,imgsize-414785.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man pays $15, finds 6.03-carat diamond worth $1M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134660969.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jack Pearadin, a dedicated Navy reservist from Missouri, has transformed his passion into a treasure hunt since 2013 at Arkansas's Crater of Diamonds State Park. Recently, his persistence paid off when he discovered a stunning 6.03-carat yellow diamond he estimates could be worth $1 million. Throughout his adventurous quest, Pearadin has unearthed over 300 gems, sharing the profits from his latest find, aptly named the 'American Dream,' with a friend.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arkansas-gem-hunter-found-a-6-03-carat-yellow-diamond-after-paying-15-to-search-a-state-park-he-says-it-could-be-worth-1-million-but-another-appraisal-puts-it-closer-to-250000/articleshow/134660969.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arkansas-gem-hunter-found-a-6-03-carat-yellow-diamond-after-paying-15-to-search-a-state-park-he-says-it-could-be-worth-1-million-but-another-appraisal-puts-it-closer-to-250000/articleshow/134660969.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134660986,imgsize-388585.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dad built a backyard coaster, now selling it for NZ$4,500]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134660199.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In the midst of the COVID-19 lockdown, inspired by a flurry of YouTube tutorials, Bjorn Burton took on an exciting challenge—he built a roller coaster in his backyard. With his father’s help, he engineered this thrilling ride after rigorous safety trials with concrete bags. Now that the neighborhood kids have outgrown it, Bjorn is ready to sell the coaster, already envisioning a future project for when he welcomes grandchildren.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-auckland-father-built-his-children-a-backyard-roller-coaster-from-scratch-during-lockdown-after-testing-it-with-90kg-of-concrete-he-is-now-selling-the-entire-setup-for-nz4500/articleshow/134660199.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-auckland-father-built-his-children-a-backyard-roller-coaster-from-scratch-during-lockdown-after-testing-it-with-90kg-of-concrete-he-is-now-selling-the-entire-setup-for-nz4500/articleshow/134660199.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T23:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134660257,imgsize-474906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[American chestnut returns to Bronx Zoo after 120 years; 25 saplings planted in NYC]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134712629.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The American chestnut is returning to the Bronx Zoo more than 120 years after blight was first documented there. The zoo and New York Restoration Project planted 25 hybrid saplings as part of a restoration effort. Once abundant across eastern North America, the tree was devastated by disease that killed nearly 4 billion trees.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/american-chestnut-returns-to-bronx-zoo-more-than-120-years-after-blight-was-first-documented-25-hybrid-saplings-planted-on-265-acre-grounds-nyc-expands-1000-tree-restoration-drive-after-disease-killed-nearly-4-billion-trees/articleshow/134712629.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/american-chestnut-returns-to-bronx-zoo-more-than-120-years-after-blight-was-first-documented-25-hybrid-saplings-planted-on-265-acre-grounds-nyc-expands-1000-tree-restoration-drive-after-disease-killed-nearly-4-billion-trees/articleshow/134712629.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T22:33:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134712933,imgsize-285500.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida's Burmese pythons are carrying three previously unknown RNA viruses]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134701715.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/floridas-burmese-pythons-are-carrying-three-previously-unknown-rna-viruses-scientists-are-investigating-whether-they-could-reach-native-snakes/articleshow/134701715.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/floridas-burmese-pythons-are-carrying-three-previously-unknown-rna-viruses-scientists-are-investigating-whether-they-could-reach-native-snakes/articleshow/134701715.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T16:50:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134702413,imgsize-1713573.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MIT revives Bill Freeman's three-sided zipper after 40 years in a garage]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134700364.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-1985-bill-freemans-three-sided-zipper-was-rejected-and-left-in-his-garage-40-years-later-mit-revived-it-as-a-shape-shifting-fastener/articleshow/134700364.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-1985-bill-freemans-three-sided-zipper-was-rejected-and-left-in-his-garage-40-years-later-mit-revived-it-as-a-shape-shifting-fastener/articleshow/134700364.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134700698,imgsize-1309843.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California scientists grow kelp in labs at 74,000 spores per millilitre]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134703291.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/california-scientists-grew-kelp-in-a-lab-at-74000-spores-per-millilitre-they-are-now-planting-the-young-forests-back-into-the-ocean/articleshow/134703291.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/california-scientists-grew-kelp-in-a-lab-at-74000-spores-per-millilitre-they-are-now-planting-the-young-forests-back-into-the-ocean/articleshow/134703291.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T17:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134703721,imgsize-136683.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists found at least 10 likely new species of bizarre branching worms inside sea sponges]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134706217.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers have identified ten likely new species of branching marine worms found within sea sponges. These unusual worms exhibit a unique tree-like body structure, which has evolved over time. Genetic analysis and museum specimens helped resolve the long-standing classification issues of these marine organisms. The study indicates these worms' diversification relates closely to their sponge hosts and geographic locations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-found-at-least-10-likely-new-species-of-bizarre-branching-worms-inside-sea-sponges-one-was-hiding-in-a-museum-specimen-collected-in-japan-in-1914/articleshow/134706217.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-found-at-least-10-likely-new-species-of-bizarre-branching-worms-inside-sea-sponges-one-was-hiding-in-a-museum-specimen-collected-in-japan-in-1914/articleshow/134706217.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T00:30:00+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134706710,imgsize-236215.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Taylor Sheridan bought a 600-acre Texas ranch as a family home; it is now a film set, horse hub and concert venue]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134711878.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Taylor Sheridan's Bosque Ranch in Weatherford, Texas, has transformed into a prominent site for film and TV productions. Originally intended as a family residence, it now generates substantial income through shows like Yellowstone and 1883. The ranch doubles as an equine center, celebrating Western culture with competitions and housing over 150 horses, making it a hotspot for equestrian training. Sheridan's strategic expansions have added to his impressive property portfolio.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/taylor-sheridan-bought-a-600-acre-texas-ranch-in-2013-as-a-family-home-years-later-bosque-ranch-is-a-film-and-tv-production-base-equine-competition-hub-and-concert-venue-with-more-than-150-horses/articleshow/134711878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/taylor-sheridan-bought-a-600-acre-texas-ranch-in-2013-as-a-family-home-years-later-bosque-ranch-is-a-film-and-tv-production-base-equine-competition-hub-and-concert-venue-with-more-than-150-horses/articleshow/134711878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T21:37:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134712053,imgsize-433332.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Five adopted Black children abused by white parents awarded $4.4 million settlement after CPS failures]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134711529.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Five adopted Black children who endured horrific abuse and neglect at the hands of their white adoptive parents have been awarded a $4.4 million settlement from West Virginia following alleged CPS failures. Some children were forced to live in a shed without running water or a bathroom before authorities discovered them in 2023.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/five-adopted-black-children-abused-by-white-parents-awarded-4-4-million-settlement-after-cps-failures-in-west-virginia-some-were-forced-to-live-in-a-shed-with